# Who must approve a change to what. With "Require review from Code Owners"
# on the main ruleset, a pull request that touches one of these paths cannot
# merge without the owner's approval, whoever wrote it.
#
# These are the files that decide what may reach AWS, what it may cost, and
# what an agent may do. Everything else needs the same one approval anyway
# while there is one maintainer; this file is what keeps these paths the
# owner's when there are more.

/.github/                                @sasha720709
/.claude/                                @sasha720709
/CLAUDE.md                               @sasha720709
/infra/bootstrap/                        @sasha720709
/infra/org/                              @sasha720709
/infra/scripts/                          @sasha720709
/infra/main/allowed-resource-types.txt   @sasha720709
/scripts/check_plan.py                   @sasha720709

# Since 2026-11-22 (docs/ROADMAP.md, 2g) a pull request that touches none
# of this file's paths and passes CI and the agent's review may merge to
# staging with no person involved. So this list is now also "what an agent
# may not change by itself", and it is wider:

